Calling a procedure declared in this file C-style is provably a dispatch
bypass (diag.direct_procedure_call, error, on the name). DoProc is the
correct form and does not fire.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE AddTax;
	:PARAMETERS nAmount;
	:RETURN nAmount * 1.2;
:ENDPROC;
:PROCEDURE Checkout;
	:PARAMETERS nNet;
	:DECLARE nGross;
	nGross := AddTax(nNet);
	nGross := DoProc("AddTax", {nNet});
	:RETURN nGross;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE AddTax;
	:PARAMETERS nAmount;

	:RETURN nAmount * 1.2;
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE Checkout;
	:PARAMETERS nNet;
	:DECLARE nGross;

	nGross := AddTax(nNet);
	nGross := DoProc("AddTax", {nNet});

	:RETURN nGross;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
8:12-8:18 error direct_procedure_call: Custom procedures cannot be called directly. Use DoProc("AddTax", {args}) for same-file script procedures, ExecFunction(...) for external script procedures, or Me:/Base: inside classes.
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
8:12-8:18 error direct_procedure_call: Custom procedures cannot be called directly. Use DoProc("AddTax", {args}) for same-file script procedures, ExecFunction(...) for external script procedures, or Me:/Base: inside classes.
